  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HYDRO REST IN MARISMAS NACIONALES BIOSPH</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will restore 5,048.68 acres of wetlands in the Teacapn-Agua Grande Tidal System located in the Marismas Nacionales Biosphere Reserve; restore 2,274.87 acres of uplands in the watershed of the Marismas Nacionales Biosphere Reserve through reforestation, which will reduce eutrophication in coastal wetlands; and evaluate habitat quality (hydroperiod, productivity, aquatic vegetation), and assess habitat use by waterfowl, shorebirds, and other aquatic birds.</narrative>
  </description>
